<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ad Decimum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">533</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandalic-war">Vandalic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ad Decimum was fought on 13 September 533 at the tenth milestone south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, where the Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> defeated the Vandal army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a>. Gelimer's attempt to trap the invaders failed, and Belisarius entered Carthage two days later. It opened Justinian's reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> from the Vandal Kingdom.</p></div>
